# First Lua Mod Guide

This is a short walkthrough for making your first Lua mod in sm64coopdx.  
We’ll start with the absolute basics and end with a working mod you can actually play.

## 1. Where mods go

You can put a single `.lua` file in either of these places:

- The `mods` folder next to the game executable
- The save location:
  - Windows: `%appdata%/sm64coopdx/mods`
  - Linux: `~/.local/share/sm64coopdx/mods`
  - macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/sm64coopdx/mods`

You can also just drag and drop the file onto the game window.

If you want multiple scripts in one mod later, make a folder and put a `main.lua` inside it.

